course: dictionary
lesson: 11553
title: Amplitude: the size of a wave
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A wave is a line that goes up and down, like the waves on the sea or the wiggles of a sound. The amplitude of a wave is how far it rises from its middle line. Think of amplitude as the size of the wave.
explain: «The loud drum made a wave with a high amplitude.» A high amplitude means the wave goes far up and down, so the sound is loud. «The soft whisper made a wave with a small amplitude.» A small amplitude means the wave is short, so the sound is quiet.
explain: Scientists use amplitude for light too. «The bright torch had a large amplitude.» A bigger amplitude means brighter light. Amplitude tells you about size, while pitch, how high or low a sound is, is linked to frequency instead.
fact: Amplitude means the size of a wave: how far it rises from its middle line.
fact: In sound, bigger amplitude means louder.
fact: In light, bigger amplitude means brighter.
fact: Amplitude can also mean large size or plenty, in a formal way.
fact: Pitch, how high or low a sound is, is linked to frequency, not amplitude.
exercise: «The loud drum made a wave with a high amplitude.» What does high amplitude tell us about the sound? | It has no sound at all | It is quiet | *It is loud | It is too short to hear
exercise: What does a bigger amplitude mean for a sound? | Quieter | Higher pitch only | Slower | *Louder
exercise: What is the amplitude of a wave? | The colour of the light | The time it takes to finish one wave | The number of waves in one second | *How far it rises from its middle line
test: «The soft whisper made a wave with a small amplitude.» What does small amplitude mean? | *The wave is short, so the sound is quiet | The wave has no middle line | The sound is very high pitched | The wave is tall, so the sound is loud
test: «The bright torch had a large amplitude.» What does large amplitude mean for light? | Light with no waves | *Brighter light | Dimmer light | Slower light
exam: Which word means large size or plenty, in a formal way? | Middle line | *Amplitude | Pitch | Frequency
